  "_version": "1.0.0",
  "_description": "Azure Entra ID (formerly Azure AD) sign-in event → AKSI control ID mapping. Entra ID is the dominant identity provider for the Microsoft 365 + Azure ecosystem and possibly the largest enterprise IdP overall. Microsoft Graph /auditLogs/signIns and /auditLogs/directoryAudits are the canonical evidence of who-signed-in, which Conditional-Access policies fired, what risk Microsoft observed, and which authentication method was used. Mapping is risk-event / risk-level / Conditional-Access / clientAppUsed driven, with overlays for legacy-auth detection (IMAP/POP/Exchange ActiveSync etc. — Microsoft itself recommends blocking these), non-compliant device on resource access, password-only authentication on privileged resources, unknown-app authentication, and cross-country / multi-app patterns. PII redaction: userPrincipalName reduced to email-domain only, userDisplayName to length+sha256, ipAddress masked to /16 IPv4 / /32 IPv6, deviceDetail.deviceId truncated to last 8, location reduced to countryOrRegion only (city / state / geoCoordinates dropped — too granular for evidence). userId is captured verbatim because Microsoft Graph object IDs are pseudonymous by design.",
